{"id":"tatnai","name":"Tatnai","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:tatnai"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Tatnai","text":"Gift, a Persian governor (Heb. pehah, i.e., “satrap;” modern “pasha”) “on this side the river”, i.e., of the whole tract on the west of the Euphrates. This Hebrew title pehah is given to governors of provinces generally. It is given to Nehemiah (5:14) and to Zerubbabel (Hag. 1:1). It is sometimes translated “captain” (1 Kings 20:24; Dan. 3:2, 3), sometimes also “deputy” (Esther 8:9; 9:3). With others, Tatnai opposed the rebuilding of the temple (Ezra 5:6); but at the command of Darius, he assisted the Jews (6:1-13)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H8674","lemma":"תַּתְּנַי","xlit":"Tattᵉnay","gloss":"Tattenai, a Persian","kjv":"Tatnai","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H8370","lemma":"שְׁתַר בּוֹזְנַי","xlit":"Shᵉthar Bôwzᵉnay","gloss":"Shethar-Bozenai, a Persian officer","kjv":"Shetharboznai","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H3675","lemma":"כְּנָת","xlit":"kᵉnâth","gloss":"{a colleague }","kjv":"companion","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H6347","lemma":"פֶּחָה","xlit":"pechâh","gloss":"{a prefect }","kjv":"captain, governor","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H5675","lemma":"עֲבַר","xlit":"ʻăbar","gloss":"{properly, a region across","kjv":"beyond, this side","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H5103","lemma":"נְהַר","xlit":"nᵉhar","gloss":"a river, especially the Euphrates","kjv":"river, stream","count":4,"share":1}],"verses":["Ezra.5.3","Ezra.5.6","Ezra.6.6","Ezra.6.13"],"related":[{"id":"shethar-boznai","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":1,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"temple-the-second","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.022,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"apharsachites","type":"lexical","strong":"H8674","why":"both lead with תַּתְּנַי (H8674)"},{"id":"shethar-boznai","type":"lexical","strong":"H8674","why":"both lead with תַּתְּנַי (H8674)"}],"works":[]}
